<article class="env-definition" id="0GXE">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GXE">Definition <span data-tag="0GXE">87.7.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a linearly topologized ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $A$ is <em>weakly pre-adic</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001560265" id="a0001560265-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if there exists an ideal $I \subset A$ such that the closure of $I^ n$ is open for all $n \geq 0$ and these closures form a fundamental system of open ideals. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $A$ is <em>weakly adic</em> if $A$ is weakly pre-adic and complete<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001560283" id="a0001560283-mark"><sup>2</sup></a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>